# 🔴 4. There's a genuine JavaScript bug in your DO interpretation

This one is important.

Your code currently says:

```javascript
if (doPercent < 60) messages.push('⚠️ Low DO — aquatic life stressed');
else if (doPercent < 40) messages.push('🚨 Critical DO — fish kills likely');
```

The `<40` condition can **never execute**.

Why?

Because if DO is 35%, it is already `<60`, so the first condition fires and JavaScript never gets to the `else if`.

### Correct order:

```javascript
if (doPercent < 40) {
  messages.push('🚨 Very low DO — severe aquatic stress; follow workplace response procedures');
} else if (doPercent < 60) {
  messages.push('⚠️ Low DO — may stress aquatic life');
} else {
  messages.push('✅ DO not flagged by this teaching model');
}
```

And I'd avoid **"fish kills likely"** because the simulator isn't sophisticated enough to make that determination.

